Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> eXcel wrote:
>
>> then bless and
>> read those that could be useful with the right equipment later, mostly
>> low-level utility spells. Identify or Remove Curse, for example.
>
> No spellbook of ID, don't recall whther I have the spell of RC, but
> I don't think so. The most useful that I can cast may be Force Bolt,

A barbarian can't enhance any missile weapons to multi-fire but they can
enhance attack school to skilled.  That tells me that a late game
barbarian will want to use attack spells for ranged combat.  That in
turn tells me that a mid-game barbarian might choose to prepare for that
by collecting armor that helps spell casting and start practicing the
skill.

Force bolt is the only level 1 attack school spell. As such
it's the one to practice with. On any level where you're sure there
are no sleeping nymphs take up casting a few force bolt spells at
approaching monsters.  Do that until you run low on energy or get
hungry.

The only good news for someone driven to play a barbarian as a spell
caster is the way spellbook gifts work when praying at altars.  For a
player at XP=N the game tries N times to randomly generate a book in a
school you do know in a spell you do not know.  With only one school
known you're likely to get attack books from prayer.  Is it worth altar
camping for the books?  Probably not.

> Meanwhile I've read all level 1-3 spells but abstained from the higher
> level spells, which seems risky to read at a success rate of about 50%.

While alone a failure rate is not a bad thing.  I've run high level
valkyries who identified everything at their liesure.

> I'll full-ID the latter and bless the books not before my attack skill
> is getting Skilled - which may never happen. Before that proficiency
> the Cold and Fire spells are at 100% failure.

While in combat failure rate is critical.  It's nice to cast at a line
of attacking monsters as they approach, but it's more effective to
retreat to a corridor.

> Well, I advanced my barbarian's Int to 10, got a robe from a friendly
> priest (after dispute with and convinced by my purple worm); the rate
> of failure is still horrible, even with GDSM and robe, and no shield,
> no GoPs.

If you've got the armor go for it.  Shirt, GDSM, robe, speed boots,
dexterity gloves, brilliance helmt, no shieid, "oR.  That and XP=30 will
get you a zero failure rate in a couple of attack spells.  Chortle. 
That and XP=30 will also get you the Amulet and slower energy recovery!

> I was in hope for Magic Missile. Currently trying hard to enhance the
> attack spell a bit using Force Bolt.

Exactly.

> (Where were all those spellbooks when I played a Wizard?!)

The RNG mocks all of us!


